out.push(A('**b** ⚠ **That they tried to have the statement altered.** **It is true and the expert was right, which is why the temptation is strong** — **and a sentence of that kind turns a professional question into an allegation, in a letter the other side may eventually read.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the seventh mediation of Book 2 and the only one in which two correct answers were in direct opposition.** **The representative asked the question he is paid to ask; the expert answered the question he is paid to answer; both held.** **Do not let the room make the representative a villain** — **and do not let it make the expert a hero either, because the expert\'s ground was not that the paragraph might help.** ⚠ **Then protect the room from the wrong lesson, which is the whole reason Pair B of the practice exists.** **The paragraph turned out to assist the party that wanted it removed, and the room will conclude that candour pays.** **It paid here.** **On Pair B it costs, and the ground for keeping the sentence is identical** — **so run both cards, in that order, and say the sentence out loud: the paragraph would have had to stay even if it had cost them the case.**'));
