out.push(SAMPLE(['Mrs Khoury said the instructing party gets the letter and it is two paragraphs: the first says that the paragraph stays and why it now assists them, and the second asks for the 2017 correspondence, which their own office holds, and offers a supplement before anybody has asked for one. Mr Zahreddine said what must not be said is that they tried to have the statement altered, and that is exactly it, and the temptation is strong because it is true and because the expert was right, but a sentence of that kind turns a professional question into an allegation, in a letter the other side may eventually read. Mrs Oueidat said the representative was doing his job, and Mr Attar said he asks the question he is paid to ask and the expert answers the question he is paid to answer, and nobody here is at fault, and this is the sixth time in Book 2 and the only one in which two correct answers were in direct opposition and both held. Dr Qabbani said and the figure helps them, and it helps them and he did not know it would: a landing poured to a hundred and sixty-three shows that the slab was poured to specification somewhere, so the shortfall at the eleven bays is workmanship and not design, which is the client\'s whole case. Mrs Khoury said the room must not take the wrong lesson, because the argument for keeping the paragraph was never that it might turn out to help, but that a statement with a hole in it is worth nothing to the party that paid for it, and the paragraph would have had to stay even if it had cost them the case. Mrs Rizk asked whether he tells them it helps them now, and Mrs Oueidat said he tells them in one sentence with the other expert\'s own words quoted, because a representative who learns from the other side\'s report that his own expert was right has learnt it in the worst possible order. Mr Tayara asked about the 2017 correspondence, and he asks for it and says that he did not ask for it before, which is already in paragraph 2 of the statement, and that is the whole value of having declared it. Mrs Tarabishi asked whether the supplement could damage the client, and Mrs Khoury said it could, and the letter says so in the same sentence that offers it. Mr Shihabi asked whether the other expert comes out of this well, and Mrs Oueidat said he comes out of it exactly as he should and nobody expected to say so. And Mr Zahreddine said the thing he will take away is the fifteenth of October and not the twenty-ninth.']));
