out.push(A('**1** **did not occur to me to**   **2** **is not possible to establish**   **3** **No more than**   **4** **made use of**   **5** **have no intention of estimating**   **6** **declined to remove**'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Part 4 is marked in two halves and candidates in this class lose the second half: one mark for the structure the key word forces and one for the rest of the sentence.** **At 1 accept _did not occur to me to_ only** — **and a candidate who writes _never occurred to me to_ has changed the tense pattern and loses the half.** **At 2 accept _is not possible to establish_ or _is not possible to ascertain_.** ⚠ **At 3 the whole item is the fixed phrase and _No more than_ is the only answer; _Not more than_ changes the meaning to a maximum.** **At 5 accept _have no intention of estimating_ only; _do not intend to estimate_ does not use the word given.** **At 6 accept _declined to remove_, and note that the item tests nothing but the complementation of the key word, which is how Part 4 gives away two of its six marks to candidates who read the word before the sentence.**'));
