out.push(A('⚠ **Part 1 is marked on the ground for the choice, on development and on the final comparison, and this class now loses marks only on the last of the three.** **The sample names the two points, gives one ground for both, and drops the first point entirely.** **Then look at what the closing paragraph does: a procedure against a disposition, with the cost of each** — **which is the move both 16.7\'s and 17.7\'s samples make, and the three should be read side by side at the end of the unit.** ⚠ **And note the concession in the middle of the third-point paragraph.** **_A reader will sometimes do exactly that._** **A Part 1 essay that takes a point and never names its cost reads as advocacy, and the examiner\'s band for development asks for exactly that sentence.**'));
